gers are pretty reliant on him reaching the end zone. Pitts and the rest of the Falcons' offense will have a good chance to get back on track in Week 9 against the Bengals' inconsistent defense.","source":"RotoWire"}]},"status":{"id":"1","name":"Active","type":"active","abbreviation":"Active"}},"source":{"id":"1","description":"basic/manual","state":"basic"},"type":{"id":"0","name":"INJURY_STATUS_ACTIVE","description":"active","abbreviation":"A"}},{"id":"645493","longComment":"Penix endured a career-worst all-around game in rainy conditions after coming into the afternoon with just one interception in his first five games. Only two of Penix's four picks led to Buccaneers points -- and just a pair of field goals at that -- but the Falcons defense was helpless against Tampa Bay's ground attack in the shutout. Sunday's conditions were a clear outlier, so Penix should be expected to bounce back across the pond in a Week 9 matchup against a vulnerable Bengals secondary next Sunday in Madrid.","shortComment":"Penix completed eight of 24 passes for 125 yards with no touchdowns and four interceptions while rushing five times for 11 yards in the Falcons' 16-0 loss to the Buccaneers on Sunday. He also fumbled once but recovered.","status":"Active","date":"2026-11-02T02:20Z","athlete":{"firstName":"Michael","lastName":"Penix Jr.","displayName":"Michael Penix Jr.","shortName":"M. Penix Jr.","links":[{"language":"en-US","rel":["playercard","desktop","athlete"],"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360423/michael-penix-jr","text":"Player Card","shortText":"Player Card","isExternal":false,"isPremium":false},{"language":"en-US","rel":["stats","desktop","athlete"],"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/stats/_/id/4360423/michael-penix-jr","text":"Stats","shortText":"Stats","isExternal":false,"isPremium":false},{"language":"en-US","rel":["stats","sportscenter","app","athlete"],"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showClubhouse?uid=s:20~l:28~a:4360423&section=stats","text":"