runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/fagnano_throw_log.md:33:- **Came in cold, 2Q ~9:40, after Huntley's toe injury.** His first two throws worked: Cuevas 15 and Lane 13, both under 1-man pressure. Then the pocket collapsed: 3 sacks in 2Q (L.Jackson, T.Parker, Rousseau), two of them on 5-man rushes and one on a 4-man rush.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/fagnano_throw_log.md:38:  - The Banner: BAL was pressured on 55% of dropbacks (NGS) by a 'blitz-happy' BUF rush that came in 2nd-to-last in pressure rate. Fagnano also treated a lower-leg injury and was 'optimistic' about Thursday.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/report.md:15:- Off-read passes (singles only, not on the card): Strange rec yds o35.5 FD -114 (4/4, OK); Washington rec u4.5 DK -125 (3/4, OK); BTJ rec u1.5 DK -195 (3/4, OK); plus downgraded Meyers/Hunter unders. See policy_legs.csv.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/report.md:17:  - Washington rec u4.5 is DROPPED from the off-read list. The Hamilton reason is "not counted", Washington is the WR1, and the leg is DOWNGRADE once Wk8 is left out.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/report.md:18:  - Washington overs FAIL 3-of-4. The o39.5/o29.5 mirror rungs pass only without Wk8, at -332/-610 (short-price flag). Candidate only.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/report.md:22:  - Washington u4.5 stays OFF. His overs miss §3, so they are a Rico decision only.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/report.md:27:  - Washington's main rec-yds line is **o63.5 FD -114** (policy_legs.csv already uses 63.5). The "o62.5 DK -112" in addenda 3 and 4 was DK's alternate quote.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/report.md:32:- The 1Q legs are downgraded and come from a thesis the blitz data weakens (see below), so they're singles only.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/report.md:68:**Thesis test.** I verified both JAX numbers against pbp+FTN: blitz rate 30.4% and pressure proxy 21.5% (Weeks 1-8, n=270 dropbacks). Fagnano had 3 sacks on 24 dropbacks.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/report.md:69:- Against Rico's blitz idea: Fagnano was **better when blitzed** (50% completions, 5.2 YPA, 0 INT) than when not blitzed (44%, 3.1 YPA, 1 INT).
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/report.md:70:- For the pressure idea: 2 of his 3 sacks came when blitzed, and the proxy shows 3 sacks on 9 pressured dropbacks.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/report.md:71:- Net: blitz rate alone doesn't back the 1Q/1H case, the sack and pressure angle does, and the sample is 1 game. The 1Q legs clear §3-of-4 on JAX's own margins, not on the Fagnano read.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/report.md:92:- BTJ-as-WR1 is REFUTED: he's a depth target. Washington is the one who fits the WR1-left pattern, which CONFLICTS with the Washington under.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/fagnano_profile.md:2:Source: nflverse play_by_play_2026.parquet (CC-BY 4.0) + nflverse FTN charting (n_blitzers, n_pass_rushers; FTN data via nflverse, CC-BY-SA 4.0). Local copies are in r2/src, pulled 2026-11-02.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/fagnano_profile.md:3:- Blitz = FTN n_blitzers > 0 (24/24 charted).
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/fagnano_profile.md:4:- Pressure = PROXY (sack OR qb_hit OR qb_scramble). **FTN has no is_qb_pressured field (MISSING)**, and true pressure isn't in pbp. Because the proxy includes sacks, it overstates how bad things look under pressure.
runs/2026-11-05_JAX@BAL_r5/fagnano_profile.md:6:- PFF cross-check only: under-pressure rating 51.3 (PFF definition). Our proxy rating is 45.1 (2/6, 22 yds, 0 TD, 0 INT). Different definitions, so the two are not comparable.
